{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836302",
      "title": "Manipulating the DOM via Refs",
      "sourceHash": "129027108f07def848a09e3062aad493d84a0c5c41bd9053093abeb5e42a81a4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 3.36,
          "en": "So as you could see in the previous lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.36,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "refs can be really useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "But what if you now want to clear this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 10.41,
          "en": "whenever we set a name?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.41,
          "end": 12.063,
          "en": "What if you wanna reset it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "Well, you could theoretically in 'handleClick'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 20.79,
          "en": "again use 'playerName.current',",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.79,
          "end": 23.913,
          "en": "so this input element which is stored in that ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 27.813,
          "en": "and then set value equal to an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 31.05,
          "en": "That would clear it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 35.043,
          "en": "If I save that and I now click 'Set Name', it gets cleared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.81,
          "end": 40.23,
          "en": "And you can now argue whether that's good or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.23,
          "end": 42.24,
          "en": "because you must not forget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.24,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "that React is about writing declarative code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 51.44,
          "en": "And it's about not directly manipulating the DOM yourself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.45,
          "end": 54.003,
          "en": "Instead, you wanna let React do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "Now, here in line nine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 60.9,
          "en": "we're already crossing that line a little bit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.9,
          "end": 63.87,
          "en": "but here we are just reading a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.87,
          "end": 66.273,
          "en": "We're not changing anything in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 72.56,
          "en": "But here in line 10, we definitely have imperative code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.75,
          "end": 75.57,
          "en": "We're not in the declarative world anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.57,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "Instead, we're clearly instructing the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 81.723,
          "en": "to set the value of that input to an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.65,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "And we're therefore basically violating that rule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "or that idea, that React should handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 92.85,
          "en": "all those DOM interactions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.85,
          "end": 95.67,
          "en": "Nonetheless, for a use case like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 98.28,
          "en": "where you just clear an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.28,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "which is then not really connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "to any other state or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 106.5,
          "en": "you can definitely consider writing code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 110.673,
          "en": "Because overall it allows you to save a lot of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 114.57,
          "en": "But you should definitely be careful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.57,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "that you don't start using refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 120.872,
          "en": "to read and manipulate all kinds of values on your page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.872,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "because that's really not the idea behind React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "But if you can make your life easier as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 131.46,
          "en": "using refs can be a great alternative to using state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.46,
          "end": 133.833,
          "en": "and all these other mechanisms you learn about.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}